.TH ADDWATERMARK 1 "2026-08-02" "addwatermark 2.1.1"
.SH NAME
addwatermark \- compatibility wrapper for imgmod watermark
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B addwatermark
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIwatermark\fR \fIinput\fR \fIoutput\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B addwatermark
applies an image watermark to an input image. It preserves the legacy argument
order while delegating processing to
.BR imgmod (1)
and its
.B watermark
plugin.

For new scripts, use
.B imgmod watermark
directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-a " opacity"
Set watermark opacity. The default is \fI0.5\fR.
.TP
.BI \-g " gravity"
Set watermark placement gravity. The default is \fISouthWest\fR.
.TP
.B \-h, --help
Show usage help.
.TP
.BI \-r " geometry"
Resize the finished image using ImageMagick geometry.
.TP
.BI \-s " percentage"
Set watermark size as a percentage. The default is \fI12%\fR.
.TP
.B \-v, --version
Show the command name and version.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B imgmod
Provides the watermark implementation and its image-processing dependencies.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Apply \fIlogo.png\fR to \fIphoto.jpg\fR:
.nf
.B addwatermark logo.png photo.jpg photo-watermarked.jpg
.fi
.TP
Use a centered, opaque watermark:
.nf
.B addwatermark -g Center -a 1 logo.png photo.jpg output.jpg
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imgmod (1),
.BR imgmod-watermark (1)
